WEBVTT

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:05.080
They say that if you give a plant beer
rather than water,

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:08.880
the plant will absorb the nutrients
from the beer and grow strong.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.840
One shimmering, shiny cocktail.

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:39.550
Its recipe consists of orange juice,
lemon juice and pineapple juice.

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:44.060
As you no doubt realise,
this is just a simple mixed juice.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:46.350
However, if you select your ice carefully,

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:49.810
consider how long to shake
to completely mix the ingredients,

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:55.530
the result is a non-alcoholic cocktail
called the Cinderella.

00:01:57.190 --> 00:01:59.360
This is how bars prepare cocktails

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:04.410
for ladies who are not strong drinkers
or cannot drink at all.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:07.750
So, this evening,

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.500
for you ladies who find it a little
intimidating to set foot in a bar,

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:16.880
we would be most pleased if you mustered
the courage to push open that door.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:25.560
Should I make you something

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:27.680
before your husband arrives, miss?

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:31.190
Yes, please. That sounds good.

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:32.310
In that case...

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:41.740
It was only a few years ago that she first
entered a bar, after I invited her.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:47.660
Welcome.

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:55.800
Initially she was strangely uninterested,
saying bars were where old men drink.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:59.970
But now my best friend is
completely hooked on them.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.470
Sayo Yasuda was her maiden name.

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:04.930
Now she goes by Sayo Yamaguchi.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:10.940
Unfortunately, both families were
totally against their marriage.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:15.270
But seeing those two sealing their bond,
as if they were eloping,

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:18.940
was such a beautiful sight to us,
their friends.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.820
They met at Eden hall.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:25.700
And tonight is...

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.500
Oww!

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:32.920
Are you alright, miss?

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:34.960
Thank you.

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:41.510
You know, it's my first time coming
to a real bar like this one,

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:43.220
my nerves must have got to me.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:47.680
Truth is, I'm staring at 30 group dates
that have gone just terribly.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:51.810
And now that I've finally made it
to a one-to-one date,

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:53.940
just Iook at me...

00:03:55.860 --> 00:04:00.230
He said a great lady
looks beautiful sat at a bar,

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:02.990
so I suggested we go to a bar
for our first date.

00:04:03.110 --> 00:04:04.990
A great lady?

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:07.530
He loves films.

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:09.910
His favourite actress is Ingrid Bergman.

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:12.410
His idea of a great lady
from a golden age.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:16.750
Which is why I really wanted
to give off that impression.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.090
Don't you worry.

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:21.340
This bartender will help you, for sure.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.050
Will you really?

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:26.140
Got that, Mr Sasakura?

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:28.930
You'll take good care of
this young lady, right?

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:32.560
If the guy's a jerk, make sure
he gets a Bloody Caesar.

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:33.600
Well, erm...

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:35.390
Bloody Caesar?

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:38.690
I've heard of the Bloody Mary...

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:44.110
There are two drinks young ladies who
can't hold their liquor should be wary of.

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:52.040
Their names come from two deceased rulers,
Mary Queen of England and Julius Caesar.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:55.160
Because they both appear to be
simple tomato juice,

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:58.880
they went unnoticed and were therefore
popular drinks in Frohibition America.

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:02.510
The difference is that the Caesar uses
tomato juice with clam broth,

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:04.920
a tomato juice called CIamato.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:08.760
And a vodka that is particularly strong,

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:14.100
either Spirytus or Balkan, which is
shaken to mix in lots of air.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:17.060
Doing this tempers the taste,

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:19.610
meaning one only faintly notices
the high alcohol content.

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:22.320
But when one drinks too many...

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.490
I suddenly feel sleepy...

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:31.490
Sorry I'm late!

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:38.580
And so began Yuka's bar debut through
which she had hoped to bring an end

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.460
to her date losing streak. But...

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:47.760
They say you can judge a man
and a woman's relationship

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:50.890
by their body language, distancing,
and dress sense.

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:54.100
But with these two...

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:56.390
Your orders?

00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:57.770
-Champagne!
-Beer.

00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:02.150
-I'll have a beer actually!
-I'll have champagne actually!

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:10.110
Champagne and beer are both
nice at this time of year.

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:12.700
But how would you feel about cider?

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:13.950
Cider?

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:17.200
Yes. The French consider it a wine,

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:20.250
but in Normandy and Brittany
they cannot grow grapes.

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:25.420
So, from long ago, they let apples
ferment to create a sparkling wine,

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:27.050
commonly known as cider.

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:28.880
Sure!

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:31.720
That sounds great.

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:37.680
Enjoy.

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:43.400
It's so refreshing and fruity.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:47.280
The flavour is different from wine

00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:49.650
and the acidity from the apples
gives it a freshness!

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:55.870
-Erm...
-Erm...

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:58.000
<i>-What to talk about...?
-What to talk about...?</i>

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:07.130
What do we do?
Those two are totally mismatched.

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:11.130
At times like these, it's a good idea to
speak to each one individually, but...

00:07:11.550 --> 00:07:12.970
I'll be back in a sec.

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:20.020
Come on Yuka!
Find something interesting to say.

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:22.060
He looks bored out of his mind.

00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:25.610
I'm a terrible date.

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:29.990
I have no idea what to say
to please a woman.

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:32.400
There's no need to try too hard.

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:34.950
Just be yourself.

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:36.660
How about...

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:39.700
Here goes. Give it all you've got!

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:42.460
Right! It was Calvados.

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:44.880
You guys sound like you're having fun.

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:49.460
A camisole...

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:55.390
<i>Perfect, it worked!</i>

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:59.970
We were just talking about this Calvados.

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:03.810
Ingrid Bergman drank it
in "Arch of Triumph".

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:05.980
Indeed.

00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:10.860
The lead actor saves her just as she is
about to throw herself into the Seine.

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:14.700
And to lift her spirits,
he offers her a Calvados.

00:08:16.820 --> 00:08:21.330
You sure are knowledgeable.
Because it's about Ingrid Bergman, right?

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:26.330
Well, I've known about Calvados
for a long time, actually.

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:32.760
It is an apple brandy made by
distilling the cider you just tasted.

00:08:34.970 --> 00:08:37.640
Add some lemon juice and
pomegranate syrup.

00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:40.180
Today, I managed to get a hold
of some fresh ones so

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:41.810
I added pomegranate juice.

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:48.400
The gentleman and I
thought of this together.

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:53.070
Please, enjoy this Jack Rose.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:56.530
Such a beautiful rose colour.

00:08:57.320 --> 00:08:59.910
The gentleman thought it would match
the red of your watch-strap.

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:01.990
I couldn't agree more.

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:05.790
You took notice of such a small detail?
That's so lovely.

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:08.540
Yeah...

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:14.090
Even our bartender here has made
all sorts of connections

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:16.090
when serving us these drinks.

00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:18.470
I'm so glad we Ieft it up to you.

00:09:28.270 --> 00:09:29.940
Hey! Look, Iook!

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:36.450
You like red, do you, Yuka?

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:37.610
I do...

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:43.950
<i>This is bad. lf he notices, all the effort
that got them this far will be wasted,</i>

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:51.840
<i>Very clever...</i>

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:53.090
You don't say.

00:09:57.380 --> 00:09:58.840
<i>It's getting chilly in here.</i>

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:05.890
Huh? You're wearing a band aid?

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:08.600
Yeah... It's just a scratch.

00:10:09.390 --> 00:10:10.150
I know.

00:10:10.850 --> 00:10:12.980
You must have fallen over again.

00:10:16.190 --> 00:10:18.740
You're always getting cuts and grazes.

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:21.740
You're like a mischievous little kid.

00:10:24.330 --> 00:10:26.450
Well, excuse me for causing mischief!

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:30.460
We all know I'll never be
a great lady, anyway!

00:10:37.630 --> 00:10:38.800
If I may make a suggestion...

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:42.890
Why don't you now enjoy the aromas
of Calvados, together?

00:10:50.890 --> 00:10:55.400
It reminds me of the sweet scent
of biting into an apple.

00:10:56.570 --> 00:11:00.240
You're right.
We got apples to snack on as kids.

00:11:01.820 --> 00:11:07.040
Starting with cider from Normandy,
a red band and a red Jack Rose.

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:10.370
The great lady, Ingrid Bergman,

00:11:10.660 --> 00:11:12.920
and the Calvados from Arch of Triumph.

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:16.460
One might say that
portraying great service

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:19.260
as though it were a coincidence is
part of running a bar.

00:11:20.590 --> 00:11:25.930
But, just like cuts and grazes and
the memories brought up by apples,

00:11:26.310 --> 00:11:29.350
love also sometimes
springs out of coincidence.

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:35.020
I'd expect no less from
the Glass of the Gods.

00:11:35.690 --> 00:11:37.360
The perfect service.

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:40.900
Not at all. It was mere coincidence.

00:11:42.530 --> 00:11:44.070
If you say so.

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:47.240
But, I wonder if those two
will really make it.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:49.950
-Thanks for a great evening!
-Thanks for a great evening!

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:55.130
Are you okay?

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:57.250
I'm so clumsy...

00:11:57.590 --> 00:12:00.590
She's always in such a rush.

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:03.130
Brings back memories, though.

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:07.050
I was a bit Iike that when
I started going to bars.

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:10.220
This is Sayo Yasuda.

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:12.390
It's her first time at this sort of bar.

00:12:13.190 --> 00:12:16.440
We're getting more ladies through
the door these days, you know.

00:12:16.980 --> 00:12:22.820
I just have no idea what I should
order in a place Iike this.

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:25.780
How about a cocktail that's
"made for Sayo", then?

00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:27.820
But what does that...?

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:30.790
That isn't a problem.

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:34.290
Leave it to the bartender
to make you the perfect drink.

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:36.250
He isn't a pro for nothing.

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:45.220
<i>I couldn't believe it.</i>

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:50.640
<i>You were so sexy.</i>

00:12:51.430 --> 00:12:52.680
Again with the flattery.

00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:57.270
From that day I became hooked on bars.

00:12:58.480 --> 00:13:00.610
And I met the man of my life.

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:04.320
It was thanks to you that we got together.

00:13:06.150 --> 00:13:08.200
Is your husband well?

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:09.870
I guess.

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:13.040
Our timetables never match.

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:16.710
We only just miss each other
even in the house.

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:21.460
I know, can you make me that cocktail?

00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:26.550
The valentine's chocolate I made
after taking a day off work.

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:29.550
But it broke on the train,
and I didn't know what to do.

00:13:30.430 --> 00:13:31.470
Then...

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:33.140
Don't fret.

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:35.230
I can bring it back to life.

00:13:37.770 --> 00:13:40.230
First, we mix chocolate in with some milk,

00:13:40.360 --> 00:13:42.230
making sure it doesn't come to the boil.

00:13:42.570 --> 00:13:45.150
You can then add some cream
to taste, if you wish.

00:13:46.150 --> 00:13:49.030
You would normally
use brandy in this cocktail,

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:53.410
but for Valentine's day, I recommend
using the liqueur of Iove, Amaretto.

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:55.200
The liqueur of love?

00:13:56.870 --> 00:13:59.750
In the 16th century,
an artist by the name of Luini

00:13:59.880 --> 00:14:04.920
used a beautiful widow as his model to
complete a fresco of the Virgin Mary.

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:07.340
This widow crafted for Luini

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:10.180
a sweet tasting liqueur
and sent it to him.

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:13.760
It is said that this became
the root of Amaretto.

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:19.140
The gentle aroma of Amaretto riding
on the sweetness of the chocolate...

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:21.230
It is Iight but has great depth.

00:14:21.980 --> 00:14:25.320
It made our Valentine's day
simply wonderful.

00:14:25.570 --> 00:14:26.940
Resulting in marriage!

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:30.740
We were brought together in this bar.

00:14:31.490 --> 00:14:33.030
And so this day is also...

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:34.410
Miss.

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:39.210
I'm sorry I'm late.

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:41.080
Welcome.

00:14:41.710 --> 00:14:43.500
Nice to see you again, Mr Sasakura.

00:14:44.170 --> 00:14:45.050
You remember?

00:14:45.590 --> 00:14:48.010
Today's our wedding anniversary.

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:52.220
I've had dinner at the company,
so I'll have a drink to start.

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:56.470
In that case, I'll make another
Amaretto AIexander for old times' sake.

00:14:58.100 --> 00:14:59.350
Darling, here.

00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:01.480
It's my gift to you.

00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:04.690
Thank you. It Iooks pretty thin.

00:15:05.070 --> 00:15:05.820
What is it, I wonder?

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:08.780
Sorry.

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:13.700
If you don't mind,

00:15:14.570 --> 00:15:17.240
I'd like to make you a different cocktail.

00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:20.250
Sure...

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:24.670
Sorry about that, the contract's
kinda on the line.

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:28.840
I might have to head back to the office.

00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:30.260
Is that so...?

00:15:31.090 --> 00:15:32.590
Mr Sasakura... what have you got there?

00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:36.140
Well, the cocktail I'm planning on
making for you,

00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:37.680
is called Bijou in France.

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:39.270
It means "jewel".

00:15:40.140 --> 00:15:41.810
The white of the gin is for diamonds.

00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:44.020
The green of the chartreuse
is for emeralds.

00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:47.020
And the red of the vermouth is for rubies.

00:15:48.690 --> 00:15:52.280
Huh. The world's most valuable
jewels all in one glass.

00:15:53.110 --> 00:15:54.740
It sure is a pretty drink.

00:15:55.280 --> 00:15:56.870
If you give it a little more time,

00:15:57.030 --> 00:16:00.700
the colours separate more clearly,
and appear even more jewel-like.

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:04.540
Thank you, Mr Sasakura.

00:16:05.330 --> 00:16:08.130
But it's okay, this guy won't get it...

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:09.840
I won't get what?

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:12.800
I'm demanding when it comes
to liquor, you know.

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:16.800
But you don't notice much else.

00:16:17.300 --> 00:16:17.970
Huh?

00:16:18.600 --> 00:16:19.890
Mr Sasakura...

00:16:20.220 --> 00:16:22.980
made this cocktail because
he noticed something.

00:16:23.770 --> 00:16:25.230
Before I even said anything...

00:16:25.730 --> 00:16:27.270
So that you would realise.

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:33.150
The cocktail's name, Bijou.
Meaning "jewel".

00:16:36.990 --> 00:16:39.410
Someone I haven't seen in ages saw it...

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:46.540
but you failed to notice that I hadn't
worn my wedding ring in 6 months.

00:16:47.790 --> 00:16:48.920
Not puite.

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:51.710
It is the job of the bartender

00:16:52.260 --> 00:16:53.800
to be observant of patrons' hands.

00:16:55.550 --> 00:16:56.680
A happy hand.

00:16:57.010 --> 00:16:57.970
An unhappy hand.

00:16:58.550 --> 00:17:00.430
An angry hand. A jubilant hand.

00:17:00.890 --> 00:17:01.890
A deceiving hand.

00:17:02.140 --> 00:17:03.270
An accusing hand.

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:05.690
And a hand that has wiped away tears.

00:17:06.520 --> 00:17:09.310
Hands reveal innumerable emotions.

00:17:10.980 --> 00:17:13.940
All the more reason
I wanted him to notice.

00:17:14.950 --> 00:17:16.990
A single cocktaiI

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:20.200
is better than a loveless jewel, any day.

00:17:20.870 --> 00:17:21.580
Sayo...

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:25.460
Say...

00:17:27.330 --> 00:17:29.580
If hands show our emotions.

00:17:30.590 --> 00:17:32.300
How do mine look to you?

00:17:32.710 --> 00:17:33.210
What?

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:37.630
Anybody can see they show nothing.

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:41.390
But my hands are always hard at work.

00:17:42.390 --> 00:17:44.890
They work every day
so as not to lose your heart.

00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:46.310
They work tirelessly.

00:17:47.140 --> 00:17:48.270
I suppose you don't know.

00:17:48.810 --> 00:17:52.020
What your parents said
to me after the ceremony...

00:17:54.030 --> 00:17:57.650
"How did a no-good, uneducated
layabout Iike you manage to trick

00:17:57.780 --> 00:18:01.580
our precious daughter who never
wanted for anything into marrying you?"

00:18:03.740 --> 00:18:05.330
Dad said such a horrible thing?

00:18:05.750 --> 00:18:06.830
I felt so embarrassed.

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:11.290
So I had no choice but to prove
myself though work.

00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:13.250
I worked without sleep.

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:15.760
I had no time to go home.

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:20.640
It was all so that I could make you
happy with these two hands.

00:18:28.770 --> 00:18:33.650
It seems our two customers are not
aware of the Bijou's other sparkle.

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:47.330
The Amber Dream.

00:18:48.750 --> 00:18:51.370
Amber is nothing more
than fossilised tree sap.

00:18:52.130 --> 00:18:55.050
It does not have
the flamboyant sparkle of a jewel.

00:18:56.420 --> 00:18:58.380
But after tens of thousands of years,

00:18:58.800 --> 00:19:01.220
it acquires beauty like no other jewel.

00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:05.510
Its beauty comes from time.

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:09.850
Time is what is collected in this drink.

00:19:10.600 --> 00:19:12.900
Time also as long as in a dream.

00:19:13.690 --> 00:19:16.860
Perhaps, by living their lives together,

00:19:17.230 --> 00:19:19.490
men and women also get that sparkle.

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:21.780
Living their lives

00:19:22.320 --> 00:19:23.160
together...

00:19:24.910 --> 00:19:29.040
We eloped because our families were
against our marriage.

00:19:30.330 --> 00:19:33.710
Yes. Being together was our only dream.

00:19:34.460 --> 00:19:36.040
-But somehow, at some point...
-But somehow, at some point...

00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:42.470
It's me.

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:46.350
I know it's an important contract.

00:19:47.390 --> 00:19:50.600
But would you give me
just enough time to finish

00:19:51.180 --> 00:19:51.770
one cocktail ...

00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:58.650
This time right now is more precious
to me than whatever is left of my life.

00:20:09.620 --> 00:20:10.580
Forgive me.

00:20:11.330 --> 00:20:13.830
I never meant to cause you such pain.

00:20:14.250 --> 00:20:15.540
It's me who should apologise.

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:18.460
I was being so selfish without
knowing what you were going through.

00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:29.060
Coincidental service... the Amber Dream.

00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:32.730
The beginnings of a young love story.

00:20:33.770 --> 00:20:36.980
I wonder how those two
are doing right now...

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:39.400
Does it still hurt?

00:20:39.900 --> 00:20:40.690
Yeah.

00:20:41.480 --> 00:20:42.030
A little.

00:20:42.820 --> 00:20:46.410
In that case, I think
you need me to give you this.

00:20:53.960 --> 00:20:54.790
You big dummy.

00:20:55.540 --> 00:20:56.750
And so...

00:20:57.630 --> 00:21:01.170
We shouldn't call it an end,
but a "Happy Aid".

00:21:06.550 --> 00:21:12.180
RECIPE: CHARTREUSE - 20ml VERMOUTH -20ml
DRY GIN - 20ml ORANGE BITTERS - 1 dash

